**The read: Type 6, 6w7, sp/sx — confidence high.** The thesis is that Weaving's whole career is an accidental treatment protocol. She has been anxious as long as she can remember ("I don't remember not being anxious, so I don't know"), and she has twice discovered on the record that an acute physical crisis cancels her nerves — once across the *Ready or Not* shoot, after which she went off her medication, and once in an ambulance beside the *Babylon* soundstage with an IV in her arm. The tiebreaker against Type 9 is that she runs an explicit trust audit before every job ("do I trust this filmmaker? Do I trust this person?") and describes trusting the future as effortful work.

